<title>SYRIA: Syria to add to cereal storage capacity.</title>
<headline>Syria to add to cereal storage capacity.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria has approved an agreement with the Islamic Bank for Development to equip three silos to add 300,000 tonnes to the total cereals storage capacity of two million tonnes, official sources said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The official newspaper al-Baath said the Syrian parliament approved the deal, under which the Syrian government will buy mechanical and electric equipment and rent it to itself. The bank will pay the costs back to Syria.</p>
<p>Syria produces over six million tonnes of wheat, barley and lentils per year.</p>
<p>It stores around five million tonnes of cereals in the open air.</p>
</text>
